jobs.description:
At PASHA Bank Georgia, we offer a collaborative environment with an international team, competitive compensation, flexible working conditions, continuous learning opportunities, and a culture that values both people and performance.

We’re looking for proactive, detail-oriented professionals who take ownership, work well in teams, and are result-driven. Guided by our EVP principles - We Grow Together, We Keep Promises, We Go the Extra Mile - we support your growth and empower you to make an impact.

Major Duties and Responsibilities

Participate in the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of the Bank’s information security and privacy frameworks, policies, standards, procedures, and guidelines in compliance with the regulations of the National Bank of Georgia and international standards (NIST Cybersecurity Framework);
Identify information security and cybersecurity risks and propose appropriate mitigation measures;
Develop procedures and internal regulatory documentation for the administration of security systems (SIEM, Vulnerability Management, Anti-Malware, IDS/IPS, WAF, DLP, PAM, and others) and monitor their implementation;
Participate in the development and monitoring of DLP rules and controls;
Respond to information security incidents in a timely manner, participate in investigations, and implement corrective actions;
Document security breaches, assess their impact, and prepare relevant reports;
Support the monitoring of privileged access, information asset inventory, and security controls;
Prepare information security reports for management and regulatory authorities;
Support security awareness initiatives and business continuity (BCP) activities.

Qualifications Required:

Education
: Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field; professional information security certifications such as CompTIA Security+, ISO Lead Implementer, or equivalent will be considered an advantage;
Work Experience
: Minimum 3 years of experience in the Information Technology field, including at least 2 years of experience in Information Security;
Languages
: Fluent knowledge of the Georgian and English languages.

Skills and Competencies Required:

Strong analytical and critical thinking skills;
Attention to detail and a high sense of responsibility;
Results-oriented mindset with strong problem-solving abilities;
Decision-making and prioritization skills;
Strong organizational and time management skills;
Well-developed interpersonal and teamwork skills;
Effective written and verbal communication skills.

Only shortlisted candidates will be contacted. We wish you good luck.

